    │
 18 │     for x in xs {
    │              ─┬
    │               ╰── walked here; the loop's binding refers to its elements
    │
 21 │         touch(&var xs)
    │               ───┬───
    │                  ╰───── borrowed here
    │
    │ Note: a `for` binding refers to the element itself, so what the loop walks must not change until the loop ends
────╯
[E0413] Error: `xs` is passed together with a `&var` reference to it
    ╭─[ err/67_for_walked_changes/main.wip:22:22 ]
    │
 22 │         both(&var x, &xs)
    │              ───┬──  ─┬─
    │                 ╰───────── a `&var` reference
    │                       │
    │                       ╰─── a `&` reference
    │
    │ Note: while a function runs, a `&var` argument must be the only reference to its place
────╯
